+  design_decision_to_make_before_coding: 'THERE IS NO FIELD TODAY THAT DISTINGUISHES THE TWO. home.drift.json
+    carries detectedAt, operation, acknowledged, acknowledgedAt and the report; nothing records that a
+    pass has SHOWN this gate. So "second surfacing" is not observable yet, and the ticket must choose
+    how it becomes observable. Two routes, and they are not equivalent:
+
+    (a) A PERSISTED MARKER on the gate -- surfacedAt / surfacedCount. Works across processes, which is
+    the case that actually bites: `exec` refuses, the operator runs `home drift`, then `exec` again, and
+    those are three processes. It is a schema change to home.drift.json, so it needs a schema version
+    and a decision about what an old record without the field means (proposal: absent == not yet surfaced,
+    which degrades to today''s behaviour rather than to silence). It also touches ack/re-pend, which AckIsNotStaleOnArrival
